## Error Handling

### Common Error Codes

| Status | Error | Cause | Solution |
|--------|-------|-------|----------|
| 400 | Bad Request | Invalid parameters | Check request schema, validate image URL/data |
| 401 | Unauthorized | Not authenticated | Ensure user is logged in, valid session |
| 403 | Forbidden | Missing API key | Configure Replicate API key in settings |
| 429 | Too Many Requests | Rate limit exceeded (30/min) | Implement retry with exponential backoff |
| 500 | Internal Server Error | Replicate API failure | Check Replicate status, retry request |
| 503 | Service Unavailable | Replicate model cold start | Retry after 10-30 seconds |

### Error Response Format

All endpoints return errors in this format:

```typescript
{
  error: string;  // Human-readable error message
}
```

**Examples:**

```json
// 401 - Missing API Key
{
  "error": "Replicate API Key not configured on server"
}

// 500 - Replicate Error
{
  "error": "Replicate Prediction Failed: failed"
}

// 429 - Rate Limit
{
  "error": "Too many requests. Please try again later."
}
```

### Error Handling Best Practices

```typescript
const handleUtilityError = (error: any): string => {
  const message = error?.error || error?.message || 'Unknown error';

  // Rate limiting
  if (error.status === 429) {
    return 'Too many requests. Please wait a moment and try again.';
  }

  // Authentication
  if (error.status === 401 || error.status === 403) {
    return 'Please configure your Replicate API key in settings.';
  }

  // Replicate-specific errors
  if (message.includes('Replicate')) {
    return 'Image processing failed. Please try again.';
  }

  // Model errors
  if (message.includes('version')) {
    return 'Model unavailable. Please try a different model.';
  }

  return message;
};
```

